      questions: [
        { id: "pub_eng_22_q43", qNum: 43, type: "8m", mark: "8 Marks", topic: "Hints Development Story", q: "Develop the following hints into a coherent story with a suitable title and moral:<br>King Bruce of Scotland - defeated six times - hides in a cave - sees a spider - tries to climb cobweb - fails nine times - tries tenth time - reaches target - Bruce inspired - gathers army - defeats English king - frees Scotland.", ans: "<b>KING BRUCE AND THE SPIDER:</b><br>King Robert Bruce of Scotland was defeated six times by the King of England. Desperate and exhausted, he hid in a secluded mountain cave, contemplating surrender. Suddenly, he noticed a tiny spider trying to reach its web across the cave ceiling. The spider fell nine times, but without losing hope, it made a tenth attempt and successfully reached its web. Bruce was profoundly inspired by the tiny creature's perseverance. He realized: 'If a little spider can try again, why can’t I?' He rallied his scattered soldiers, fought a ferocious battle at Bannockburn, defeated the English army, and won independence for Scotland.<br><b>Moral:</b> Try and try until you succeed. / Persistence leads to victory.", markingScheme: "Title & Moral: 2M, Story: 6M = 8 Marks", isCompulsory: false },
        { id: "pub_eng_22_q44", qNum: 44, type: "8m", mark: "8 Marks", topic: "Comprehension Passage", q: "Read the passage and answer the questions that follow:<br>Discipline is the cornerstone of human life. Without discipline, neither an individual nor a society can prosper. Discipline teaches self-control, punctuality, and respect for law and order. In school life, disciplined students excel in academics and sports. In national life, disciplined citizens make a country prosperous and strong.<br>(i) What is the cornerstone of human life?<br>(ii) What does discipline teach us?<br>(iii) How does discipline help students in school life?<br>(iv) Give a suitable title to the passage.", ans: "<b>Answers:</b><br>(i) Discipline is the cornerstone of human life.<br>(ii) Discipline teaches self-control, punctuality, and respect for law and order.<br>(iii) In school life, disciplined students excel in academics and sports.<br>(iv) Title: <b>The Importance of Discipline in Life</b>.", markingScheme: "4 questions: 4 × 2 = 8 Marks", isCompulsory: false }
      ]
